&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Help make the world more hospitable &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The hospitality industry is uniquely human, and it deserves technology that’s just as inspiring as the people behind it. At Mews, we’re transforming the industry with a platform that helps hotels run smarter, move faster and create better guest experiences.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You’ll work with smart, curious people who care deeply about what they do. You’ll have autonomy and the trust to make good decisions and move quickly. And you’ll enjoy a real sense of purpose as you see the impact of what we’re building.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;If you’re motivated by ownership, curiosity and meaningful impact, and are driven to deliver consistent high performance, you’ll feel at home here.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Let&#39;s get into the specifics. It’s impossible to capture every nuance of a role – especially at a rapidly growing company like Mews – but if we had to distil it into a job description (which we do because this is a job description), it would be this:&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal&quot;&gt;You will own the Business Central ERP platform at Mews, the system that carries every transaction, journal entry and regulatory obligation across the business. Finance teams across six pillars bring precise, point-in-time problems, and engineering needs clear specifications to act on them; this role is the connection between the two. Mews is building the financial infrastructure that an audit-ready, fast-growing SaaS company needs at scale, and the shape of that is still being decided.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal&quot;&gt;You will be one of two product owners across the entire finance ERP estate, working with accounts payable, accounts receivable, controlling, general ledger, tax and reporting. That breadth is unusual: most ERP product roles cover one pillar, and this one asks you to hold the whole picture alongside the detail. You will work directly with internal Mews engineers rather than through third-party implementation partners, which means shorter feedback loops and real influence over what gets built.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal&quot;&gt;The immediate work is order. The backlog needs a clear framework for triage, sequencing and communication, and you will build it. Beyond that, you will evaluate what Microsoft ships each release cycle, turn regulatory obligations such as mandatory e-invoicing into delivery plans with dates attached, and evolve integrations with treasury and open banking infrastructure. Hospitality is scaling fast and the finance systems underneath it need to keep pace.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you would do&lt;/strong&gt; &lt;em&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/em&gt;Own and curate the Business Central backlog across accounts payable, accounts receivable, controlling, general ledger, tax and reporting&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul class=&quot;[li_&amp;amp;]:mb-0 [li_&amp;amp;]:mt-1 [li_&amp;amp;]:gap-1 [&amp;amp;:not(:last-child)_ul]:pb-1 [&amp;amp;:not(:last-child)_ol]:pb-1 list-disc flex flex-col gap-1 pl-8 mb-3 print:block print:space-y-1&quot;&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2&quot;&gt;Translate finance stakeholder requirements into clear engineering specifications, working directly with internal engineers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2&quot;&gt;Evaluate Microsoft&#39;s release cycles and incoming functionality, and decide what to adopt, configure or build&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2&quot;&gt;Turn regulatory requirements, including mandatory e-invoicing and audit-readiness obligations, into roadmap items with clear delivery plans&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2&quot;&gt;Use AI to shape the backlog itself: synthesising stakeholder requests into structured specifications, comparing release notes against current configuration, and building repeatable prompts and workflows the wider finance and engineering group can reuse&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;AI Fluency Level 3:&lt;/strong&gt; in this role that means you have already changed how requirements gathering, specification writing or release analysis gets done using AI, not just made your own drafting faster. You have built an approach other people picked up and used, and you check what the tools return: a specification that misreads a tax rule or a release summary that misses a breaking change has to be caught by you, before it reaches engineering.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal&quot;&gt;&lt;em&gt;For more information on AI fluency at Mews, please refer to &lt;a class=&quot;underline underline underline-offset-2 decoration-1 decoration-current/40 hover:decoration-current focus:decoration-current&quot; href=&quot;https://mews.atlassian.net/wiki/x/XQOskg&quot;&gt;AI Fluency at Mews: A Comprehensive Guide for Candidates&lt;/a&gt; on Confluence.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
