&lt;li class=&quot;font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2&quot;&gt;Meet with GTM teams to understand their processes firsthand, then design and ship automation that removes real manual work&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2&quot;&gt;Own delivery end to end: no PM, no handoff, you scope, build, and validate what you ship&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2&quot;&gt;Travel to local offices when deeper embedding is needed, build alongside the team for a few days, and train them on what you shipped&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2&quot;&gt;Architect systems that integrate with Salesforce, HubSpot, Nue, Databricks and Gong, with security and reliability built in from the start&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2&quot;&gt;Work as the connective layer between engineering rigor and commercial reality, translating GTM problems into production-grade AI systems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal&quot;&gt;AI Fluency Level 4: this role is built around it. You will design and ship AI-powered systems that GTM teams depend on for real commercial outcomes, not internal prototypes. That means making engineering decisions about model choice, agent design, and RAG pipelines the same way you would about any other production system, and taking full ownership of what happens when it is live.&lt;/p&gt;
